    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying a prime position on one of Ballsbridge's most highly regarded residential roads, this exceptional Victorian residence combines the elegance and character of its period origins with the scale, comfort and sophistication of a fully modernised family home. Completely refurbished and thoughtfully extended, the property provides generous and versatile accommodation over four levels, including six bedrooms, five elegant reception rooms and an impressive open-plan kitchen, living and dining space at garden level. A beautifully landscaped south-facing rear garden and extensive off-street parking for up to eight cars, framed by magnificent, mature beech trees, further enhance this outstanding home.\n\nBehind its handsome Victorian façade, the property retains a wealth of period character while providing exceptional contemporary family accommodation. At hall level, the welcoming entrance hall leads to three well-proportioned reception rooms, offering excellent spaces for formal entertaining, dining and family living, together with a butler's service area. Also at this level there is a generous study and cloakroom. Up from there off the half landing is a bright generous bedroom and family bathroom.\n\nThe top floor provides three bedrooms, two with en-suite bathrooms, while the garden level accommodates two additional bedrooms, both with en-suites. This level also features a dedicated family room, extensive storage, a wine cellar and a large utility room, together with a spectacular extended kitchen, living and dining space. Two full-height sliding doors provide a seamless connection to the beautifully landscaped south-facing garden, creating an exceptional setting for both family life and entertaining.\n\nParticular care has been taken to integrate the original house with its contemporary additions, creating a home of considerable style, scale and versatility. The generous front garden provides rare off-street parking for up to eight cars, while the mature beech trees create an impressive approach.\n\nBallsbridge is one of Dublin's most prestigious residential suburbs, renowned for its leafy streets, period architecture and exceptional convenience. The property is ideally positioned close to Herbert Park, the RDS, Aviva Stadium and the amenities of Ballsbridge, Donnybrook and Sandymount. Dublin city centre is readily accessible, while Sandymount Strand and the coast are also within easy reach.\n\nExcellent public transport links include the DART at Sydney Parade and regular bus services along the Merrion and Stillorgan Roads, with convenient access to the city's road network and Port Tunnel. A superb selection of schools is nearby, including St. Michael's College, St. Andrew's College, Blackrock College and Muckross Park College."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGeneral - \nFlight of granite steps leads to porch and\n\nEntrance Hall - \nwith marble floor, ceiling coving, centre rose, arch to inner hall\n\nDrawing Room - 5.75m x 5.1m\nwith marble fireplace, detailed cornice work and centre rose\n\nSitting Room - 4.05m x 5m\nwith matching marble fireplace and cornice work\n\nDining Room - 4.2m x 5.3m\nwith Victorian white marble chimney piece, slate hearth, window overlooking rear garden, very good ceiling coving and centre rose\n\nButler's Pantry/Cloakroom - \nwith stainless steel work surfaces and sink, wall and floor presses, mirrored splashbacks\n\nHalf Landing - \n\n\nCloakroom - \nwith built in closets and shelving, panelled wall, WC, stone vanity unit with feature whb, stone splash back and shelving, heated towel rail and stone floor\n\nStudy - 4.5m x 2.8m\nwith corner window\n\nGarden Level - \n\n\nUtility /Laundry Room - 2.8m x 3.4m\nwith oak floor, comms unit, Miele washer, Miele dryer, marble work surfaces, wall and floor presses and sink unit\n\nPlant Room - \nWith pair of gas fired central heating boilers\n\nDownstairs WC/Cloakroom - \nwith oak floor, wall hung Kohler wc, vanity wash hand basin with stone surround and mirrored splashback\n\nBedroom 5 - 5.1m x 5m\nwith fitted wardrobe, dressing table\n\nEn-Suite Shower room - \nWith shower, WC, wash hand basin\n\nBedroom 6 - 4.1m x 4.7\nwith oak floor\n\nEnsuite Shower Room - \nwith large step in shower\n\nFamily Room - 4m x 4.9m\nwith gas fired stove with stone hearth, oak floor, sliding door out to the rear garden\n\nWine Cellar - 2.8m x 1.6m\nwith CDI temperature-controlled wine fridge, floor presses and Franke sink unit with marble tops and fitted wine racks\n\nKitchen/Family Room - 9.1m x 8.1m\nwith oak floor throughout, family area with Bellfires gas stove, two sliding doors out to patio and rear garden. Kitchen area has a Miele warming tray, Miele microwave, Miele steam oven, Miele fridge, Miele freezer, Miele dishwasher, wall and floor presses, Falcon five-ring two oven gas range, kitchen by Blackrock Kitchens, Quooker tap, large centre island with stonework surfaces and splashback\n\nFirst Floor Return - \n\n\nLanding - \nwith view out over St. Michaels College\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.8m x 6.5m\nwith extensive range of built in wardrobes with fitted interiors and dual aspect view\n\nBathroom - \nwith bath, large shower, vanity wash hand basin with stone surround, WC, stone floor, stone tiling, mirrored splashback and heated towel rail\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nMain Bedroom - 5.5m x 5.1m\nwith two windows overlooking Ailesbury Road\n\nDressing Room - 4.1m x 2m\nwith built in hanging and shelving units\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 4.1m x 3.3m\nwith freestanding bath, pair of vanity wash hand basins with stone surround, large mirror splashback, large walk-in shower with raindrop head, WC, stone tiled floor.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.4m x 5.1m\nwith extensive range of wardrobes with fitted interiors\n\nEnsuite Shower Room - \nwith vanity wash hand basin, wc, shower with raindrop head, stone tiled floor and walls\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.4m x 3.7m\nwith built in wardrobe\n\nOutside - \nThe front garden is a notable feature of the property, approached via a generous gravel driveway providing off-street parking for up to eight cars. The driveway is framed by two magnificent specimen beech trees, with mature hedging and planting providing privacy and a particularly attractive setting. Granite steps lead to the front entrance, while a side gate provides access to the rear garden and garden level. Useful under-stairs storage is also provided.The private south-facing rear garden is beautifully landscaped and provides an ideal setting for outdoor entertaining and family enjoyment. A stone-paved patio leads to raised planted borders and steps ascending to a well-maintained lawn. Mature trees, shrubs and hedging surround the garden, creating a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion, while a timber garden shed provides additional storage.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Outstanding period residence extending to approx 497 sqm / 5,353 sqft</li><li> A stunning combination of contemporary flair and classical Victorian elegance</li><li> Five beautiful reception rooms</li><li> Six generous bedrooms, five en suites</li><li> Utterly secluded south facing garden</li><li> Ample off-street car parking for approximately eight cars</li><li> One of Dublin's premier addresses located in the heart of Ballsbridge Dublin 4</li><li> Fitted carpets & blinds included</li><li> Gas fired central heating, underfloor at garden level.</li><li> Wiring for alarm and CCTV systems</li><li> Site area 0.22 acre</ul>"
